                %li
                  %a{:href => "#via_holographic_light_front_qcd"} Via holographic light front QCD
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Hadron supersymmetry (
            %a{:href => "#Miyazawa66"}> Miyazawa 66
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Miyazawa68"} Miyazawa 68
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry+breaking"} dynamically broken
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
            among the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/experiment"} experimentally
            observed spectra of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hadrons"} hadrons
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetry"} symmetry
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+hadrodynamics"} quantum hadrodynamics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/masses"} masses
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mesons"} mesons
            (which are
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bosons"} bosons
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryons"} baryons
            (which are
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fermions"} fermions
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tetraquarks"} tetraquarks
            (which are again
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bosons"} bosons
          %p
            This experimentally observed (see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Phenomenology"} below
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavor+physics"} flavor
            supersymmetry is in contrast to the more popular but also more speculative idea of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/color+charge"} color charge
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+QCD"}> super QCD
            ,
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MSSM"} MSSM
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quarks"} quarks
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gluons"} gluons
            have
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superpartners"} superpartners
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/squarks"} squarks
            and
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gluinos"} gluinos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quarks"} quarks
            have never been observed, due to their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/confinement"} confinement
            inside
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hadrons"} hadrons
          %p
            A model of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/confinement"} confined
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
            which brings out the hadron supersymmetry is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+light+front+QCD"} holographic light front QCD
          %p
            In terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+engineering+of+QFT"} geometric engineering of QFT
            via
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersecting+D-brane+models"} intersecting D-brane models
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hadron+supersymmetry"} hadron supersymmetry
            means that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavor+brane"} flavor brane
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetric
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/color+brane"} color brane
            may not be.
          %h2#theory Theory
          %p
            From the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constituent+quark+model"} constituent quark model
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hadrons"} hadrons
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+chromodynamics"} quantum chromodynamics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hadron+supersymmetry"} hadron supersymmetry
            follows (
            %a{:href => "#CattoGuersey85"}> Catto &amp; Gürsey 1985
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#CattoGuersey88"} 1988
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                both single
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/antiparticle"} anti
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quarks"} quarks
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi q
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar q
                as well as
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diquarks"} diquarks
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi q
                      %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                      %mi q
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q\!q
                carry the same
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/color+charge"} color charge
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mn 3
                          %mo ¯
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi Rep
                          %mi ℂ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi SU
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 3
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi c
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{\mathbf{3}} \in Rep_\mathbb{C}(SU(3)_c)
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/color+charge"} color charge
                predominantly determines the properties of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bound+states"} bound states
                in
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
            %li
              %p
                the exchange of anti-quarks with diquarks inside the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bound+state"} bound state
                with yet another
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quark"} quark
                exchanges
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mesons"} mesons
                with
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryons"} baryons
          %p
            this gives an approximate
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetry"} symmetry
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/confinement"} confined
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
            as shown on the left here:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mtext antiquark
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mtext diquark
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mphantom
                            %mi q
                          %mover
                            %mi q
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↔
                        %mtd
                          %mphantom
                            %mi q
                          %mi q
