                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\text{antiquark} &amp; &amp; \text{diquark}
                  \\\
                  \\phantom{q} \bar q &amp; \leftrightarrow &amp; \phantom{q} q\!q
                  \\\
                  q \bar q &amp; \leftrightarrow &amp; q q\!q &amp; \leftrightarrow &amp; \bar q\!\!\bar{q} q\!q
                  \\\
                  \\text{meson} &amp;  &amp;\text{baryon} &amp; &amp; \text{tetraquark}
                  }
          %p
            Dually, both
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quarks"} quarks
            as well as
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/antiparticle"} anti
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diquarks"} diquarks
            carry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/color+charge"} color charge
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 3
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi Rep
                      %mi ℂ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi SU
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 3
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{3} \in Rep_\mathbb{C}(SU(3)_c)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryons"} baryons
            with
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tetraquarks"} tetraquarks
          %p
            These transformations organize into a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
            operation, successively relating
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mesons"} mesons
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryons"} baryons
            and
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tetraquarks"} tetraquarks
          %figure{:style => "margin: 0 0 0 0"}
            %img{:src => "/nlab/files/HadronSupersymmetry.jpg", :width => "600px"}/
            %figcaption{:style => "text-align: center"}
              from
              %a{:href => "#NielsenBrodsky18"} Nielsen  Brodsky 2018
          %p
            In the formulation of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/confinement"} confined
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
            as
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+light+front+QCD"} holographic light front QCD
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hadron+supersymmetry"} hadron supersymmetry
            is brought out explicitly by the fact that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/light+cone+gauge"} light cone quantum mechanics
            of the system refines to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetric+quantum+mechanics"} supersymmetric quantum mechanics
            (
            %a{:href => "#dTDB14"}> dTDB 14
            , see e.g.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#NielsenBrodsky18"} Nielsen &amp; Brodsky 2018
          %p
            This
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
            would be an exact
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetry"} symmetry
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+hadrodynamics"} quantum hadrodynamics
            if
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti-particle"} anti
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quarks"} quarks
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diquarks"} diquarks
            had not only the same
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/color+charge"} color charge
            but also the same
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass"} mass
            (and other properties), for instance if the quarks involved all had vanishing mass, as assumed, to lowest order, in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chiral+perturbation+theory"} chiral perturbation theory
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetry+breaking"} breaking of the symmetry
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry+breaking"} supersymmetry breaking
          %p
            %br/
          %h2#Phenomenology Phenomenology
          %p
